    "Serving DHCP and DNS means adding a temporary address to a network interface and listening on ports 53 and 67. Only a privileged helper can do that. Dnsmasq for Mac itself never runs with administrator rights.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "提供 DHCP 与 DNS 服务需要向网络接口添加临时地址，并监听 53 与 67 端口。只有特权 helper 才能完成这些操作。Dnsmasq for Mac 自身永远不会以管理员权限运行。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
